WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.140
Arkansas sued kalshi, seeking restitution, penalties, and an injunction over sports bets. This is prediction

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:12.720
markets daily, episode 44. Journalism and education, never a bet, a token recovery proposal,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.940
a new data sharing deal between the futures regulator and the agriculture department, and a

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.460
segment on futures prices as forecasts. A day after other state cases against the exchanges

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.820
were already on this show, Arkansas filed its own. The block reported the suit on November

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.840
4th. Attorney General Tim Griffin says Kalshi built a global business that lets people

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.320
bet on the outcome of almost anything. And the state says money on a sporting event

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.740
is gambling in substance no matter what label sits on the contract.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:47.180
Arkansas says the company pulled in users there without the licensing, oversight, and limits

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.460
that gambling operators have to meet. Griffin also says Kalshi knows the platform can push

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.520
people into excessive betting, financial losses, depression, and other mental health harms.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:03.260
KRK reported that the same attorney general sued the gaming platform VGW as well.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.380
What exists so far is a filing, not a judgment.

00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:12.672
Binance and Polymarket have asked Polygon to hard fork stolen tokens back, trading view

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:19.412
reported, after Binance's record $6.3 billion hack on October 29th, and a separate incident

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:23.772
in which Polymarket paused trading because a third-party provider had been compromised.

00:01:23.772 --> 00:01:30.912
A Wednesday governance proposal covers about $70.49 million POL, roughly $6.8 million,

00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:34.172
sitting in five addresses the attacker controls.

00:01:34.832 --> 00:01:42.532
Of that, $23.86 million POL, about $2.31 million, sits across four addresses tied to the

00:01:42.532 --> 00:01:50.632
polymarket hack, and $46.63 million POL, about $4.51 million, sits in one address tied to

00:01:50.632 --> 00:01:51.452
the Binance hack.

00:01:51.452 --> 00:01:56.712
The fork would strip those balances at a chosen block and credit the same amounts to recovery

00:01:56.712 --> 00:02:01.912
wallets the two companies designate, once ownership of those wallets is verified, and

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:04.092
POL's total supply would not change.

00:02:04.652 --> 00:02:08.072
Block producers are already refusing transactions from those addresses.

00:02:08.692 --> 00:02:13.672
The proposal itself calls that freeze temporary and says it cannot hand the coins back.

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:18.292
Governance still has to approve it and it still has to be tested on the AMOI testnet.

00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:24.415
discussion was set for November 5th, no main net date is confirmed. The Commodity

00:02:24.415 --> 00:02:27.895
Futures Trading Commission and the Department of Agriculture announced a

00:02:27.895 --> 00:02:31.955
memorandum of understanding on November 4th, aimed at the integrity of

00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:36.335
American farm markets. The agreement is supposed to line up policies, share

00:02:36.335 --> 00:02:41.575
information, widen access to risk management tools, and help both agencies watch

00:02:41.575 --> 00:02:45.775
for structural or systematic risks. Chairman Michael S. Selig said the

00:02:45.775 --> 00:02:50.475
partnership should tighten protections for farmers, ranchers, and producers through cleaner

00:02:50.475 --> 00:02:51.175
data sharing.

00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:56.815
Secretary Brooke Rollins said faster, more transparent sharing should help the two agencies spot

00:02:56.815 --> 00:02:58.855
risks and answer market events.

00:02:59.899 --> 00:03:02.539
Kalshi posted its own scorecard on the midterms.

00:03:02.979 --> 00:03:11.199
The favorite on its markets won 479 of 487 races so far, which the company called 98%, and

00:03:11.199 --> 00:03:15.739
it said that call was in before any vote was counted, and that the markets beat the polls

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:22.039
and the models. A second post said candidates priced at 50% when polls opened, one about 50%

00:03:22.039 --> 00:03:27.059
of the time, and that the same pattern showed up at the other prices on CalShi. A third

00:03:27.059 --> 00:03:31.539
post said the market's forecast better than the models, and that people know more than the

00:03:31.539 --> 00:03:37.923
experts. Those are the venues claims about its own book, not an outside audit. A US appeals

00:03:37.923 --> 00:03:43.703
court has denied CalShi's petition for a rehearing in the Nevada case. CDC Gaming reported,

00:03:43.703 --> 00:03:49.263
That denial is a court ruling on the re-hearing request in a federal appeals court in a case

00:03:49.263 --> 00:03:49.963
out of Nevada.

